    "introduction": "Christian Lees is an English actor, born in Colchester, Essex, alongside his twin brother, Jonah. He began his career on stage, notably as Gavroche in Les Misérables on London's West End. Christian transitioned seamlessly to film and television, starring in Tale of Tales, which premiered at Cannes Film Festival in 2015. He is best known for his role as Jerry Lee Lewis in CMT's Sun Records and has starred alongside Mark Rylance and Sally Hawkins in Phantom of the Open, directed by Craig Roberts. Additionally, he was directed by Danny Boyle in FX's Pistol, portraying Sex Pistols' original bassist Glenn Matlock. With a versatile portfolio spanning stage and screen, Christian continues to captivate audiences worldwide.",
